script,scripts/zm/thundergun.csc
// v1.99.21 - script,scripts/zm/thundergun.gsc REMOVED - loads from raw, see mod_base.zone.
// ============================================================================
//  🛑 THE 6 ANIMTREES AND 6 ANIMSTATEDEFS ARE NOT SHIPPED. THIS IS THE CRASH.
//
//  MEASURED: the fourth crash happened with zmqol_ww unset, i.e. ALL THREE GUNS
//  GATED OFF - only 2 raw fx loaded instead of 17, so no registration script ran
//  - and it still died at the identical point. That exonerates every line of the
//  ported script layer and leaves only assets that load unconditionally at map
//  init. These twelve are exactly that.
//
//  Black Ops 2 ships NO animtrees/*.atr or animstatedefs/*.asd as rawfile assets
//  at all - checked zm_transit, zm_transit_patch, common_zm and patch_zm, none
//  carries zm_transit_basic. So these were not overriding a stock rawfile; they
//  were introducing an asset class the map does not otherwise have, and mod.ff
//  loads before the map.
//
//  This project has already been here: zone_source/mod_locations.zone records
//  that shipping an animtree without its runtime scriptmodelsuseanimtree() call
//  made "every map die on load". Same class of failure, same symptom.
//
//  COST, stated plainly: zombies play no wonder-weapon reaction animation - no
//  thundergun fall/getup, no freeze shatter pose. They take full damage and die
//  normally, which is the same degradation the package README already accepts
//  for every special enemy. The guns themselves are unaffected.
// ============================================================================
// ============================================================================
//  v2.10.5 - THE FOUR MODIFIED TREES ARE BACK, for the four maps the guns are
//  ENABLED on (thundergun.gsc:31 / teslagun.gsc:40 / freeze.gsc gate all three
//  OFF on zm_buried and zm_tomb, so those two are deliberately NOT declared:
//  Buried keeps the STOCK pair mod_locations.zone ships for Borough, and Tomb's
//  modified copy is against an older base - 34 removed lines - so it is not a
//  clean overlay).
//
//  Why this is not the v1.69.0 crash again - measured, not hoped:
//   1. The crash condition was 'states declared, anims absent'. v1.69.1
//      declared all 102 xanims explicitly (block below); Unlinker --list on the
//      current mod.ff shows all 30 reaction anims present by name.
//   2. Pre-flight per ERROR_CATALOGUE s10: every name in each modified .atr
//      resolves in mod.ff or that map's own family of fastfiles
//      (zm_<map>, _patch, so_*). Transit family: 3441 xanims, 0 unresolved
//      beyond the stock file's own list.
//   3. Diffed against the STOCK rawfiles dumped out of so_zsurvival_zm_transit,
//      zm_nuked, zm_highrise, zm_prison: each modified .atr = stock + 41 lines,
//      each .asd = stock + 78 lines (the 30 anims / 13 states), ZERO removals,
//      and the additions are byte-identical across the four maps.
//   4. Working precedent: Treyarch ships these exact assets the same way -
//      rawfile animtrees/zm_transit_basic.atr + animstatedefs/.asd live in
//      so_zsurvival_zm_transit.ff (retail sweep of all 216 fastfiles). No
//      scriptmodelsuseanimtree() is involved for AI trees - that contract is
//      for script_models (the Wunderfizz), not actors.
//   5. mod.ff loads BEFORE the map fastfiles (console_zm.log: 'Loading fastfile
//      mod' at menu time, zm_transit + so_zsurvival at map time) and first-load
//      wins, which is exactly why v1.69.0's copy took effect and crashed.
//  Files are CRLF like stock's. Restores: Winter's Howl freeze pose + torso
//  frost + shatter/crumple, Wunderwaffe death anims, Thundergun fall/getup
//  (its srs_ww_anims_supported() gate now checks the state at runtime).
//  DEPLOYED, NOT BOOTED - if Diner dies at load with 0x80000003 and no script
//  error, THIS is the first suspect: comment the eight lines and relink.
// ============================================================================
// Stock retail files plus only the two DLC5 Moon Wave Gun states. Matching
// server/client AIType overrides provide the twelve referenced animations.
rawfile,animtrees/zm_transit_basic.atr
rawfile,animstatedefs/zm_transit_basic.asd
rawfile,animtrees/zm_nuked_basic.atr
rawfile,animstatedefs/zm_nuked_basic.asd
rawfile,animtrees/zm_highrise_basic.atr
rawfile,animstatedefs/zm_highrise_basic.asd
rawfile,animtrees/zm_prison_basic.atr
rawfile,animstatedefs/zm_prison_basic.asd
// still NOT shipped (guns gated off there): zm_tomb_basic, zm_buried_basic
// ============================================================================
//  🛑 v2.10.6 - REVERTED. BOOTED 2026-09-02 and the map refused to load with:
//    BG_AnimStateDef_Parse: state 'zm_death_tesla_t5' has subState with anim
//    'ai_zombie_tesla_death_a' that was not found in its animtree. A reconvert
//    of aitypes using this animtree is probably required. (file zm_transit_basic, line 4)
//  So the .asd rawfile IS parsed at runtime, but the anim set it is checked
//  against is the one COMPILED INTO THE AITYPE assets, not the .atr text. The
//  xanims being present in mod.ff does not matter; the aitype's own anim list
//  is what must contain them, and that is baked by Treyarch's converter (no
//  BO2 mod tools exist). This is the true cause of the v1.69.0 crash class -
//  not 'anims absent' - and it cannot be fixed by declaring assets. The
//  reaction animations are therefore NOT restorable on this toolchain unless
//  OAT can relink aitypes from source, which is the one thing left to check.
// ============================================================================
// zm_qol: REMOVED. These files exist only so the Linker walks their %anim
// references - which it does not do (see the xanim block below). With the
// modified animtrees no longer shipped, every %ai_zombie_thundergun_* they name
// is undefined in the stock tree, and the game refuses to compile:
//   Server script compile error: animation "ai_zombie_thundergun_hit_jackiespin_left"
//   not defined in anim tree "zm_transit_basic"
// script,scripts/zm/zm_tomb/anims_thundergun.gsc
// zm_qol: REMOVED. These files exist only so the Linker walks their %anim
// references - which it does not do (see the xanim block below). With the
// modified animtrees no longer shipped, every %ai_zombie_thundergun_* they name
// is undefined in the stock tree, and the game refuses to compile:
//   Server script compile error: animation "ai_zombie_thundergun_hit_jackiespin_left"
//   not defined in anim tree "zm_transit_basic"
// script,scripts/zm/zm_nuked/anims_thundergun.gsc
// zm_qol: REMOVED. These files exist only so the Linker walks their %anim
// references - which it does not do (see the xanim block below). With the
// modified animtrees no longer shipped, every %ai_zombie_thundergun_* they name
// is undefined in the stock tree, and the game refuses to compile:
//   Server script compile error: animation "ai_zombie_thundergun_hit_jackiespin_left"
